              "task": "same-second-tasks-sort-by-id-1-4",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "Create-sequence tests read stored sequences through the backfilling parser, so three no longer check what create writes",
              "failure": "If create stops assigning a sequence, the subtests named for the stored sequence still pass (backfill renumbers on read); Task 1-5 import-order checks through readPersistedTasks would pass with no implementation",
              "detail": "persistedSeqs (internal/cli/create_seq_test.go:26-33) and the slice at :67-78 read via readPersistedTasks -> storage.ReadJSONL (internal/cli/create_test.go:49-57), which now backfills; :61-80, :82-94, :124-142 pass with Seq: task.NextSeq(tasks) removed from create.go:221. Fix: decode raw seq as rawSeqs does (internal/cli/backfill_seq_test.go:23-43)",
              "files": [
                "internal/cli/create_seq_test.go",
                "internal/cli/create_test.go",
                "internal/cli/backfill_seq_test.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "same-second-tasks-sort-by-id-1-4",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "Store.Mutate rebuilds the cache from the mutated slice, not a parse of the written bytes, so an appended unnumbered task caches at seq 0 while every fresh parse backfills a number",
              "failure": "After such a write, tick list / tick ready put the unnumbered task first among same-second peers until the next write, and tick rebuild changes the listed order: the silent misordering the feature removes; reachable today via tick migrate (StoreTaskCreator assigns no seq until Task 1-5)",
              "detail": "internal/storage/store.go:193-206 writes MarshalJSONL(mutated) and calls cache.Rebuild(mutated, newRawJSONL); internal/migrate/store_creator.go:76-87 appends task.Task with no Seq. Structural fix: call backfillSeqs(mutated) in Mutate before marshalling so no write can store an unnumbered record and the cache equals a parse of the file bytes",
              "files": [
                "internal/storage/store.go",
                "internal/storage/jsonl.go",
                "internal/migrate/store_creator.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "same-second-tasks-sort-by-id-1-5",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "The sequence invariant depends on every task-creation site calling NextSeq; Store.Mutate does not backfill the mutated slice before writing and caching it",
              "failure": "Any creation path leaving Seq at 0 reproduces the fixed defect: the cache is rebuilt from the mutated slice at seq 0, the next read sees a matching hash and does not refresh, and the newest task lists first among same-second same-priority ties, silently; task.NewTask (internal/task/task.go:284) builds exactly such a task and is the obvious trap for the next creation path",
              "detail": "Running the numbering pass from internal/storage/jsonl.go:124-127 over mutated in Store.Mutate (internal/storage/store.go:188-205) before MarshalJSONL makes file and cache agree whatever the caller supplied; alternatively NewTask takes the task set and assigns NextSeq, or is deleted as dead production code",
              "files": [
                "internal/storage/store.go",
                "internal/storage/jsonl.go",
                "internal/task/task.go"
              ]
            }
          ]
